FINAL PRODUCT VISION

Veylentra Lecture Notes must not feel like a Markdown editor with an AI button attached.

It must feel like a complete educational creation and knowledge workspace.

A student should be able to:

- Photograph handwritten class notes.
- Convert them into organized digital notes.
- Correct the extracted equations.
- Add examples and explanations.
- Link the note to homework.
- Turn important concepts into flashcards.
- Generate a revision sheet.
- Export a beautiful PDF.

A teacher should be able to:

- Create structured lesson notes.
- Insert equations and diagrams.
- Upload handwritten teaching material.
- Organize chapters and subjects.
- Link notes to homework.
- Generate practice questions.
- Share authorized material with students.

And both should be able to do these things without fighting the interface.

Make the experience exceptionally simple, while making the underlying capabilities exceptionally powerful.

The objective is not merely to add features.

The objective is to make creating, organizing and learning from notes one of the best experiences in Veylentra.

Do not sacrifice reliability, mathematical accuracy, document integrity, security or the fixed PDF export for visual polish.